# SPECIALIZED SKILL 3 — WEEKLY GROWTH & PROFIT REACT SAAS

## Pre-flight (contract check)
This skill is written against the contract defined in Specialized Skill 1 (`client_id = d2c_weekly_growth`, `saas_ready: true`). `generate_react_frontend.py` must still read the real `frontend_contract.json` at run time and `sys.exit(1)` naming the missing field if `saas_ready` is not true or any path below is absent. Nothing below is hardcoded where the contract supplies it.

**One correction to the Skill 1 contract:** the Worker forecaster does a nearest-key lookup on a single number. Our forecast is a 13-week outlook, so the forecaster input is `weeks_ahead` (1-13). Set `model.input_fields = ["weeks_ahead"]` in Skill 1's `frontend_contract.json`, and have `export_for_frontend.py` emit `FORECAST_LOOKUP` as `{"1": {...}, ..., "13": {...}}` where each value is `{net_revenue, net_profit, lower, upper}`. Spend and discount what-ifs live in the DECIDE simulator (pre-computed JSON), not in the Worker.

## Client Context
A D2C seller spends on Search, Social, Email and Display, runs promotions, and tracks a weekly P&L down to Net_Profit and Cash_Balance. The SaaS turns the pipeline's outputs into a private dashboard the client owns and deploys to Cloudflare. It shows what happened (UNDERSTAND), what to do about channels and promos (DECIDE) and whether the next 13 weeks are on track (MONITOR).

## Design Decisions
`d2c_ecommerce` is not in the domain list, so I derived it from the closest match (retail) and the business's tone: numbers-first, commercial, trustworthy.
- Typefaces: **DM Sans** (headings) + **Inter** (body), via Google Fonts with fallback `system-ui, sans-serif`.
- Palette (CSS variables only, no raw hex in components): `--color-primary #14213D` (deep navy), `--color-accent #F59E0B` (amber), surface `#FFFFFF`, bg `#F5F6F8`, border `#E3E6EC`, text `#1A1A1A` / `#4A5160` / `#7A8190`, danger `#C0392B`, warning `#E67E22`, success `#27AE60`.
- Styling: **plain CSS variables + component classes in `index.css`** (no Tailwind, no CSS-in-JS), used consistently. Insight-card badges and text use explicit inline hex per spec.
- Charts: **Recharts** (Specialized Skill 3 overrides Common Skill 3's Chart.js).
- Currency: assumed `₹`, kept in one `CURRENCY` constant in `utils/formatters.js`; change it in one line if the books are in another currency.
- Terminology map (from `meta/terminology.json`): revenue = "Net Revenue", customer = "Customer", product = "Order", transaction = "Order". Defaults in `TerminologyContext` match, so a failed fetch still renders correctly.
- Business name (`project.name`) is shown in the sidebar and header on first paint.

## 3-Outcome Structure
UNDERSTAND (4 tabs)
- "This Week's Numbers" (KPICards)
- "Profit & Spend Charts" (ChartPanel)
- "Unusual Weeks" (AnomalyTable)
- "Week Types" (SegmentExplorer: Efficient / Steady / Burn)

DECIDE (4 tabs)
- "What's Happening" (InsightCards)
- "This Quarter's Actions" (RecommendationEngine)
- "What If I..." (WhatIfSimulator)
- "My Targets" (GoalTracker)

MONITOR (3 tabs)
- "13-Week Outlook" (Forecaster)
- "Target Progress" (GoalProgress)
- "My Alerts" (AlertCenter)

Sidebar order and labels come from a tab map in the scaffold script keyed by contract path, so renaming a tab is a one-line change.

## Component specializations

**Shared**
- `TerminologyProvider` / `useTerm()`: every business-concept string goes through it, including chart titles, summary lines and empty states.
- `Header`: project name, "Last updated: X hours ago" from `meta/run_log.json` (`useRunLog`), and the active segment filter ("Viewing: Burn weeks, Clear").
- `OutcomeContext`: holds the selected week-type segment; UNDERSTAND charts re-filter by it.
- `SeverityBadge`, `EmptyState`: explicit colors, no inheritance. Empty state text: "Run main.py to generate your {Net Revenue} data".

**UNDERSTAND**
- `KPICards` (`understand/kpis.json`): Net Revenue, Net Profit, Net Margin %, ROAS, CAC, LTV to CAC, Cash Balance, Cash runway (weeks). Currency 0 decimals, ratios 2, percents 1. Trend arrow vs previous 4 weeks: success color up, danger down; LTV_to_CAC card shows a warning state below 3.0 and runway below 8 weeks.
- `ChartPanel` (`understand/charts/`): titles are business questions, e.g. "Is my business growing profitably?", "Where does my marketing money go?", "Do promo weeks make or lose money?", "Is my customer acquisition paying back?", "Is my cash safe?". Time series -> LineChart, channel mix -> stacked AreaChart, promo comparison -> vertical BarChart, month x year -> custom heatmap table (Recharts has none). Reference lines at LTV_to_CAC = 3.0 and the cash-runway floor. Empty data renders `EmptyState`.
- `AnomalyTable` (`understand/anomalies.json`): columns from `Object.keys(rows[0])` with headers mapped through the terminology map; summary "N unusual weeks flagged, X% of all weeks"; each row shows the plain-English reason from Phase 6; high severity gets a red left border and badge; sortable, 20 per page, default sort severity descending.
- `SegmentExplorer` (`understand/segments.json`): three cards (Efficient, Steady, Burn) with week count, mean Net Margin, mean ROAS, mean CAC; click sets the filter in `OutcomeContext`.

**DECIDE**
- `InsightCards`: sorted HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW; filter bar uses the five categories (Channel Performance, Promo Profitability, Customer Economics, Cash & Collections, Seasonality). Explicit hex on every text element; action box starts with a verb.
- `RecommendationEngine`: cards read like "Cap Display spend: 6 weeks of rising spend with no lift in Orders" or "Repeat the {promo} promo: median Net Profit is above non-promo weeks". "Mark done" strikes the card and moves it to Completed, stored in `localStorage` inside try/catch.
- `WhatIfSimulator`: one panel per file in `decide/simulations/` (`channel_budget_shift`, `promo_discount_depth`, `cac_cap_scenarios`). The slider snaps to the nearest pre-computed key (no live math, zero-length guard). Result: impact value plus a plain sentence using `useTerm()`. If the slider is outside `observed_range`, show a visible "outside the range seen in your data" notice.
- `GoalTracker`: inputs "Weekly Net Profit target", "Weekly Net Revenue target"; defaults from `decide/goals.json`; saved to `localStorage` with try/catch; progress bar in accent color; status On track / At risk / Behind; unset shows "Set your target to track progress".

**MONITOR**
- `Forecaster`: loads `monitor/forecast.json` for the history-plus-forecast chart (band shown). Input is **Weeks ahead (1-13)**, calling `runForecast(weeks_ahead)` -> `fetch('/api')`. Result: "Expected Net Revenue: ₹X in week N (range ₹L to ₹U)" plus expected Net Profit. Spinner while loading; error text "Prediction unavailable. Ensure pipeline has run and worker is deployed."
- `GoalProgress` (`monitor/goal_progress.json`): LineChart actual vs target with a dashed projection; sentence "You are N% behind your Net Revenue target this month" built with `useTerm()`.
- `AlertCenter` (`monitor/alerts.json`): active alerts on top (revenue drop, cash runway below floor, DSO above limit, LTV to CAC below 3.0, loss-week risk). Client-editable thresholds ("Alert me if Net Revenue drops by more than X%", "Alert me if cash covers fewer than N weeks") saved to `localStorage` in try/catch, pre-filled from `goals.json`. History shows the last 30 runs from `run_log.json`.

## Deployment rules applied
- `.gitignore` written first (`node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.env`, `.wrangler/`); `.env` with `VITE_DEV_AUTH=true` written second; `.env.example` committed.
- `package.json` `name = "d2c_weekly_growth"` (contract `client_id`, unmodified; note npm names should be lowercase, which this is); dependencies as specified (React 18, react-router-dom 6, recharts), plus `wrangler` pinned as a devDependency (`^3`) as a precaution, since `[site]` Workers Sites is the legacy mechanism and newer wrangler majors may reject it. Verify against current Cloudflare docs when scaffolding.
- `wrangler.toml`: `name = "d2c_weekly_growth"` (no suffix), `main = "worker/forecaster.js"` before `[site]`, `[site] bucket = "./dist"`, `compatibility_date = datetime.date.today().isoformat()`, no `[[pages]]`, no `[env]`.
- `worker/forecaster.js`: one complete file; `getAssetFromKV` + `__STATIC_CONTENT_MANIFEST`; `/api` POST handled first; SPA fallback to `index.html` for non-asset paths; CORS headers on every `handleForecast` response, including the OPTIONS preflight (the base spec omitted OPTIONS handling, so I add it); never `env.ASSETS.fetch()`.
- `useForecast.js` uses relative `fetch('/api')`, never `VITE_WORKER_URL`.
- `AuthContext.jsx` keeps the comment about the infinite-loop risk without `VITE_DEV_AUTH=true`, and `loading` is cleared on fetch failure.
- All `fetch` and all `localStorage` access wrapped in try/catch; every chart checks for empty data.
- Scaffold script prints `npm install` as step 1 (needed for `package-lock.json`, the usual cause of Cloudflare build failure), then `npm run dev`, git commit/push, `npx wrangler secret put FORECAST_LOOKUP`, `npm run deploy`.
- Cloudflare settings in README: root directory `d2c_weekly_growth/`, build `npm run build`, deploy `npx wrangler deploy`.

